/*!
\page page_stgmtstrip StGmtStrip

\brief Raw ADC samples, pedestal, and reconstructed charge for one GMT readout strip.

\section gmtstrip_overview Overview

StGmtStrip holds per-channel data for the **GEM-based Muon Tracker (GMT)**.
The GMT has 8 modules, each with two orthogonal layers: X-strips and Y-pads.
Each channel is read out by APV25 (15 time bins).  The class stores raw and
pedestal-subtracted ADC arrays, calibration values, and electronics coordinates.

**Detector**: GEM-based Muon Tracker (GMT)  
**Stage**: Raw DAQ → pedestal subtraction → charge reconstruction

\section gmtstrip_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StGmtStrip
\endcode

\section gmtstrip_geometry Geometry

| Constant | Value |
|----------|-------|
| \c kGmtNumModules | 8 |
| \c kGmtNumStrips | 128 channels/layer |
| \c kGmtNumTimeBins | 15 time bins |

\c mIsY = 0: X-strip (spatial coordinate); \c mIsY = 1: Y-pad (orthogonal).

\section gmtstrip_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Int_t | \c mGeoId | Geometric strip ID (module × layer × strip) |
| \c Int_t | \c mModule | Module index (0–7) |
| \c Int_t | \c mCoordNum | Coordinate number within layer (0–127) |
| \c Int_t | \c mIsY | 0 = X-strip, 1 = Y-pad |
| \c Float_t | \c mPosition | Physical position relative to module origin |
| \c Short_t[15] | \c mAdc | Raw ADC time samples |
| \c Short_t[15] | \c mPedSubtractedAdc | Pedestal-subtracted ADC time samples |
| \c Short_t | \c mMaxAdc | Peak raw ADC |
| \c Short_t | \c mMaxPedSubtractedAdc | Peak ped-subtracted ADC |
| \c Float_t | \c mCharge | Reconstructed charge (C) |
| \c Float_t | \c mPed, \c mPedStdDev, \c mPedErr | Pedestal and uncertainties |
| \c Int_t | \c mIsC | 1 if strip is used in a cluster |

\section gmtstrip_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getGeoId() | Geometric strip ID |
| \c getModule() | Module index |
| \c getCoordNum() | Coordinate index |
| \c isY() | 1 = Y-pad, 0 = X-strip |
| \c getAdc(tb) | Raw ADC at time bin \c tb |
| \c getPedSubtractedAdc(tb) | Ped-subtracted ADC at time bin \c tb |
| \c getMaxAdc() | Peak raw ADC |
| \c getCharge() | Reconstructed charge |
| \c chargeValid() | True if charge is valid |

\section gmtstrip_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StGmtStrip* strip = ...; // from GMT strip collection
if (!strip->chargeValid()) continue;
int   module  = strip->getModule();
float charge  = strip->getCharge();
short maxPedSub = strip->getMaxPedSubtractedAdc();
\endcode

\see StGmtHit, StGmtPoint, StGmtCollection
*/
